{"agent":"bgt","data":{"by":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"When multiple findings in the sibling gate share the same design point (for example, two different findings reported on the same file/symbol location, but with different digests), `_sibling_copy` iterates over the list of findings and picks the first one whose digest is different from the input digest and whose verdict is unsettled. If the first finding matching the design point happens to be a completely different, unrelated finding that just happens to be on the same file/symbol and has not been triaged yet, `_sibling_copy` will incorrectly select it as the \"reworded copy\" of the triaged finding, applying the triage verdict to the wrong finding under the sibling gate.","digest":"682476ba3f15e816","family":"google","location":"ddflow/api/review/findings.py:_sibling_copy","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/review/findings.py:_sibling_copy"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The stated bug is that after the head moves, research, rules, implement, standards, bug_hunt and dedupe stay [x] because their evidence still names older blobs. This diff never reads HEAD or those gates' evidence, so that failure is unchanged: commit a new blob, leave those gates' evidence pointing at the previous blob, and status still shows them passed. The only new behavior is design-point mirroring, and the new test never constructs a moved head or a stale blob.","digest":"96da0404dd3ab708","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/review/findings.py:_sibling_copy","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/review/findings.py:_sibling_copy"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"Fallback matching drops the line and ignores the finding text, so the first unsettled sibling at the same file is treated as the same finding. Given rubber_duck digest e7a60ba901a6a3bf at x.py:44-45 (\"shells out via subprocess\") and a critic list whose first unsettled item is x.py:10 digest aaaa (\"unrelated race\") plus a later x.py:43-44 copy, `next` records refuted on aaaa and leaves 16bbaac36ff0a462 open. The regression test uses that same location collapse and would accept the mis-bind.","digest":"64ca5998980fa9b9","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/review/findings.py:_sibling_copy","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/review/findings.py:_sibling_copy"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":5329,"diff_sha":"030e42636c1ba819733c068ec21e8dffc37badf9074d623ebc3386bea63c21a1","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-Bbd391bfef5","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1.2,"family":"google","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","output_digest":"5a10a23ad6ded3d9","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bbd391bfef5.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261109T124507Z-3e555c00.jsonl","reason":"","review_id":"0a4f3048e896","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"5870349d2c000157790667e87b7b57fe8a1c53d4","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/review/findings.py":"100644 d30d4e40ca647747aa00f1cd64dc67343d4f3fee","tests/test_review_triage_combined.py":"100644 ce94140202f02de50277056f9e53b8cd0f7c7241"},"reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reviewer_digest":"c7d1b7506be569ee","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/review/findings.py:_sibling_copy","ddflow/api/review/findings.py:_sibling_copy","ddflow/api/review/findings.py:_sibling_copy"],"tree_sha":"5870349d2c00+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"e13e1cf25a382cbc8331c86b9","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":161625,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-Bbd391bfef5","ts":"2026-11-09T12:46:27.600583Z"}
